= Pavel Axelrod

Axelrod (1850-1928) is an elder of Russian Marxism and the founder of the idea of a broad workers' congress. He is the party's link to the socialists of the West.

**Western Socialist Network.** Axelrod lobbies the Western socialists for pressure and aid.

*Effect:* Soviet democracy +1; repression −1; resources +2; more pressure from the socialists abroad.

*Calling on an advisor takes the turn, and then no advisor can act again for six months.*

